      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Studies of aryl phosphonate derivatives of a butyrophilin 3A1 ligand have resulted in identification of a potent stimulant of Vγ9 Vδ2 T cells. This compound, a mixed ester bearing one pivaloyloxymethyl substituent and one 1-naphthyl ester displayed an EC50 of 0.79 nM as a stimulant of T cell proliferation, and a 9.0 nM EC50 in an assay designed to measure interferon gamma production. In both assays, this is the most potent butyrophilin ligand prodrug yet reported, and thus it should be a valuable tool for studies of T cell function. Furthermore, mixed aryl/acyloxyalkyl esters may represent a new class of phosphonate prodrugs with high efficacy."},
